All the comforting flavors of chicken parmesan packed into an easy 30-minute weeknight burger. Ground chicken is seasoned with garlic, herbs, and Parmesan, pan-seared, and finished in simmering marinara under gooey melted mozzarella.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/recipes/a49120/chicken-parm-burger-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 lb. ground chicken
- ½ cup Italian-style seasoned breadcrumbs
- ¼ cup freshly chopped parsley
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- ¼ cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 1 tablespoon vegetable or olive oil
- 2 cups marinara sauce (plus more for spreading)
- ¾ cup shredded mozzarella cheese
- 4 burger or brioche buns, toasted
- Fresh basil, thinly sliced for garnish

## Instructions

1. **Form the Patties:** In a medium bowl, combine the ground chicken, Italian breadcrumbs, minced garlic, chopped parsley, and grated Parmesan. Season generously with kosher salt and black pepper. Mix gently until just combined (avoid compacting the meat) and form into 4 evenly sized patties.
2. **Sear in the Skillet:** In a large skillet over medium-high heat, warm 1 tablespoon of oil. Add the patties and cook undisturbed until the bottoms are nicely browned, about 4 to 5 minutes.
3. **Add Marinara and Mozzarella:** Carefully flip the patties over. Pour the 2 cups of marinara sauce directly into the skillet around and between the patties. Reduce heat to medium so the sauce simmers gently without scorching. Top each patty evenly with the shredded mozzarella cheese.
4. **Cover and Melt:** Cover the skillet with a lid. Simmer for 10 to 12 minutes, or until the chicken burgers are cooked through to an internal temperature of 165°F and the mozzarella is completely melted and bubbly.
5. **Assemble the Burgers:** Spoon a spoonful of hot marinara sauce from the pan onto the bottom half of each toasted bun. Use a spatula to lift out a cheesy chicken patty onto each bun. Scatter fresh sliced basil across the cheese and cap with the bun tops.

## Notes

- **Moist Chicken Patties:** Italian breadcrumbs and grated Parmesan help bind the lean ground chicken while locking in moisture during cooking.
- **Bun Choice:** Brioche buns, ciabatta rolls, or toasted garlic bread buns make fantastic pairings.
